      },
      "worked": "Write $B$ for black and $W$ for white. With replacement and a $1:1$ colour ratio, the eight ordered colour sequences are equally likely.\n\n$$S=\\{BBB,BBW,BWB,BWW,WBB,WBW,WWB,WWW\\}.$$\n\nAt most one black marble means zero or one black marble, so the favourable sequences are $WWW$, $BWW$, $WBW$ and $WWB$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at most one black})&=\\frac48\\\\P(\\text{at most one black})&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
